# Where the Overwatch catalog comes from

Everything here was checked on **2026-10-10**. `catalog.json` is the two-kind
form (`kinds`: Heroes, then their Weapons; `../README.md`), the same shape as
Rainbow Six Siege's operators and guns (D125): the owner picks the hero he is
playing, then that hero's own weapons. It carries a `review` line (D132): the
app holds it off until the owner has checked it.

**The game's name.** Blizzard's own patch notes are titled "Overwatch 2 Retail
Patch Notes" up to December 2025 and "Overwatch Retail Patch Notes" from the
Season 1 notes of 2026-02-10 on ([Dec 2025](https://overwatch.blizzard.com/en-us/news/patch-notes/live/2025/12/),
[Feb 2026](https://overwatch.blizzard.com/en-us/news/patch-notes/live/2026/02/)),
so the pack id is `overwatch` and "Overwatch 2" is an alias.

**Pictures: every hero has Blizzard's own portrait (D472, 2026-10-24).** The
owner decided on 2026-10-24 to show the real official hero art in the AI
Scripts room; the licence question is his, for later. The table at the end
says where each one came from. Weapons still have no picture (class code).

