  allies and damages enemies") and **Mizuki** (Spirit Glaive, "bouncing
  projectile that damages enemies") are the first ability on each page, as a
  weapon normally is; the previous `uncertain` notes are cleared. Guides
  (mobalytics.gg, screenhype) also call Spirit Glaive his primary fire.
- **Sombra**'s Season 5 rework keeps her Machine Pistol (on her page today).
  **Roadhog** was reworked the same day and keeps the Scrap Gun (on his page).
- The previous catalog cited gameluster.com, pcgamer.com and
  windowscentral.com for D.Mon, Shion and Doctrine; those are replaced by
  Blizzard's patch notes for the same season.

**Marked `uncertain` (2):** D.Mon's Plasma Saber and Fusion Repeater: the page
names both, but which of the three the HUD shows when is not known without a
real frame.

Ids: a hero's starts with his role (`tank.d_va`, `support.lucio`), a weapon's
with its hero's role (`support_weapons.caduceus_blaster`). The weapons kind is
called `hero_weapons` so the app says "weapon", not "gun".

## HUD states

From public guides and Blizzard's pages, **not checked on a real frame**.
Positions are for the default HUD at 1080p; players can scale or hide HUD
parts, so the player's own box matters.

| State | What is on screen | What the Core could read |
|---|---|---|
| Hero select / hero swap | Full-screen hero gallery; the chosen hero's name in large text and their portrait | The hero, once, by its name or portrait; the cleanest moment to learn who is being played (also after every mid-match swap) |
| In play | Hero portrait and health bar bottom-left; ability icons and ammo count bottom-right; ultimate meter bottom-centre; crosshair centre | The hero by its portrait or ability row (no name as text); the weapon only where its icon or ammo counter changes (the ten heroes above); ammo count as digits |
| Scoped | Widowmaker's and Ana's scope overlay, Freja's Take Aim, Sojourn's charge; the HUD dims or is covered | That the player is scoped (the overlay itself); little else |
| Ultimate active | Ability row changes (Genji's Dragonblade, Bastion's Artillery, Mercy's Valkyrie, D.Va's mech gone after Self-Destruct); some ultimates change the whole screen | That the ultimate is live, from the ultimate icon or the changed ability row |
| Dead / kill cam | Kill cam replay from the killer's view, then a respawn timer; the HUD shown is the killer's | Nothing of the player's own: the Core must treat it as "not in play", or it will read the killer's hero |
| Spectating / round transition | Assemble / setup timers, round-won banners | Nothing to act on |
| Menus | Main menu, perk choice (mid-match), scoreboard (Tab), Stadium's Armory between rounds, settings | Nothing to act on; perk menu and scoreboard cover the HUD mid-match |

**Font:** Blizzard's own italic display face, used for names on the select
screen only.

## Class: Rainbow-style

Overwatch is **Rainbow-style** (character-picker driven, like Siege's
operators): the Core is taught each hero's picture (the portrait or the
ability row, D122), and the weapon's picture only for the ten heroes whose
HUD changes with the weapon. Evidence: in play the HUD prints **no weapon
name and no hero name** as text (only ammo digits and ability icons); every
hero has a fixed, unique kit, so knowing the hero is knowing the weapon; the
only screen with the hero's name as text is hero select, which is a
character picker. Name-reading would have nothing to read in play, and the
game is not a "pass" because the hero changes everything an AI Script needs.

## Update the list when a season adds a hero

1. Open the season's patch notes
   (`https://overwatch.blizzard.com/en-us/news/patch-notes/live/<yyyy>/<mm>/`)
   and the new hero's page on overwatch.blizzard.com/en-us/heroes/.
2. Check each hero's role on the heroes page too: Sombra changed role in
   Season 5, so a role can move. A hero who moves gets a new id in the new
   role's group (only while nothing has shipped; after that, ids never change).
3. Add the hero at the end of his role's group, with `loadout.weapons`, and
   each weapon at the end of the role's weapon group with `usedBy` naming him.
4. Set `asOf` and `season`, then run `node dashboard/tools/test-game-data.js`.

